From: ProsperoMC contributors
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: forward PS5 wheel ticks through the existing input queue

Mouse-motion code 0 keeps its existing meaning; code 1 sends a Windows wheel
event. The queue accepts motion events already, so ntdll needs no ABI change.

--- a/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
@@ -569,3 +569,10 @@
         case 2:
-            move_cursor( hwnd, event.x, event.y );
+            if (event.code == 1)
+            {
+                INPUT wheel = {.type = INPUT_MOUSE};
+                wheel.mi.dwFlags = MOUSEEVENTF_WHEEL;
+                wheel.mi.mouseData = event.y;
+                NtUserSendHardwareInput( hwnd, 0, &wheel, 0 );
+            }
+            else move_cursor( hwnd, event.x, event.y );
             break;
